.TH KIRKWARE 1 "September 2026" "kirkware 1.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kirkware \- native Linux runtime and diagnostics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kirkware
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kirkware
provides the native Linux application runtime, settings, filesystem diagnostics,
supported Steam/Garry's Mod discovery and launch integration, and a testable
in-process Linux component lifecycle.
The preserved Windows runtime remains separate.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show command-line help.
.TP
.B --version
Print the Linux port version.
.TP
.B --paths
Print resolved XDG and application paths.
.TP
.B --settings
Print effective Linux runtime settings.
.TP
.BI --set " KEY=VALUE"
Persist a validated Linux runtime setting. The option may be repeated.
.TP
.B --reset-settings
Restore default Linux runtime settings.
.TP
.B --game-info
Search known Steam roots and Steam library folders for Garry's Mod app ID 4000.
.TP
.B --launch-game
Request a normal Garry's Mod launch through Steam, falling back to the desktop Steam URI handler.
.TP
.BI --component-self-test " SO"
Load the cooperating Linux component shared object into the current process,
validate its ABI, poll its health status, and shut it down cleanly.
.TP
.B --check
Run filesystem and runtime health checks.
.TP
.B --no-workspace
Skip temporary workspace creation for this invocation.
.TP
.B --keep-workspace
Keep the temporary workspace after normal process exit for this invocation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kirkware/linux.conf
Native Linux settings file. If XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset, ~/.config/kirkware/linux.conf is used.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/kirkware/logs/kirkware.log
Runtime log. If XDG_STATE_HOME is unset, ~/.local/state/kirkware/logs/kirkware.log is used.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kirkware/workspaces
Temporary locked workspaces when XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is available.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/kirkware/libkirkware_component.so
Default system installation location for the Linux in-process component on systems using /usr/lib as the library directory.
.SH SETTINGS
The supported linux.conf keys are keep_workspace, cleanup_stale_workspaces, and workspace_retention_hours.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR steam (6),
.BR xdg-open (1)
